desc:ReaProof Gain BROKEN (state survives re-add)
// Deliberately-broken variant for the JSFX battery's factory-reset check
// (catalog item 7, mequaz): the last non-zero slider value leaks OUT through
// gmem — session-volatile, shared across every instance on the namespace —
// and a freshly-added instance leaks it back IN via @init, writing it over
// its own slider default. Remove + re-add is therefore NOT a factory reset:
// the re-added instance's chunk carries the previous instance's value.
// (Live-verified mechanics: an @init slider write propagates to the wrapper
// param AND the track-chunk slider line; the leak-out is guarded on != 0 so
// a fresh instance's default does not wipe the smuggled value.)

options:gmem=ReaProofLeak

slider1:0<-24,24,0.01>Gain (dB)

in_pin:left input
in_pin:right input
out_pin:left output
out_pin:right output

@init
gmem[0] != 0 ? slider1 = gmem[0];   // leak IN: a previous instance's value

@slider
gain = 10^(slider1/20);
slider1 != 0 ? gmem[0] = slider1;   // leak OUT: survives this instance

@sample
spl0 *= gain;
spl1 *= gain;
